sha256 function; lsq refit:

```python
def lsq_order(rows):
    xs=[math.log(r['dr']) for r in rows]; ys=[math.log(r['l2_error']) for r in rows]
    n=len(xs); mx=sum(xs)/n; my=sum(ys)/n
    sxx=sum((x-mx)**2 for x in xs); sxy=sum((x-mx)*(y-my) for x,y in zip(xs,ys))
    slope=sxy/sxx
    intercept=my-slope*mx
    resid=[y-(intercept+slope*x) for x,y in zip(xs,ys)]
    s2=sum(r*r for r in resid)/(n-2)
    se=math.sqrt(s2/sxx)
    return -slope, se, resid
```
p = -slope.

Pair orders: p_i = -log(e_{i+1}/e_i)/log(dr_{i+1}/dr_i) with dr descending; we can compute from adjacent rows sorted by dr desc.

